{"name":"Golden Gate","hex":"#d9c09c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Golden Gate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The strait that connects San Francisco Bay to the Pacific Ocean.","Ellipsis of Golden Gate Bridge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Golden_Gate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Gate","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Gate is a strait on the west coast of North America that connects San Francisco Bay and the Pacific Ocean. It is defined by the headlands of the San Francisco Peninsula and the Marin Peninsula, and, since 1937, has been spanned by the Golden Gate Bridge. The entire shoreline and adjacent waters throughout the strait are managed by the Golden Gate National Recreation Area."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Wpdms_usgs_photo_golden_gate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Gate","wikidata":"Q220032"},{"title":"Golden Gate (Jerusalem)","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Gate or Gate of Mercy is the only eastern gate of the Temple Mount, and one of only two Gates of the Old City of Jerusalem that used to offer access into the city from the East side."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Gyllene_porten.jpg/330px-Gyllene_porten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Gate_(Jerusalem)","wikidata":"Q1367167"},{"title":"Gate","blocks":[{"text":"A gate or gateway is a point of entry to or from a space enclosed by walls or other barriers. The word is derived from Proto-Germanic *gatan, meaning an opening or passageway. Synonyms include portal. The concept originally referred to the gap or hole in the wall or fence, rather than a barrier which closed it. Gates may prevent or control the entry or exit of individuals, or they may be merely decorative. The moving part or parts of a gateway may be considered \"doors\", as they are fixed at one side whilst opening and closing like one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg/330px-Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gate","wikidata":"Q53060"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg/500px-Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg/1280px-Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg/500px-Golden_Gate_with_fog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fog rolls into San Francisco Bay through the Golden Gate, almost obscuring Alcatraz Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGolden_Gate_with_fog.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Satellite_view_of_fog_over_the_Golden_Gate.jpg/500px-Satellite_view_of_fog_over_the_Golden_Gate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Satellite_view_of_fog_over_the_Golden_Gate.jpg/1280px-Satellite_view_of_fog_over_the_Golden_Gate.jpg?utm_source